LangGraph will teach  the fundamental idea of agent orchestration and stateful workflows.

Then ADK will show how to build agents in the Google/Gemini ecosystem.

===========


LangGraph & ADK which one I have to select my project?


| Your project requirement        | Choose                   |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------ |
| Simple chatbot                  | Neither may be necessary |
| RAG chatbot                     | RAG framework/library    |
| One AI Agent + tools            | **ADK or LangGraph**     |
| Complex conditional workflow    | 🟢 **LangGraph**         |
| Many workflow branches/loops    | 🟢 **LangGraph**         |
| Multi-agent system              | 🟢 **Either**            |
| Gemini + Google Cloud           | 🔵 **ADK**               |
| Vertex AI / Agent Platform      | 🔵 **ADK**               |
| Google Cloud deployment focus   | 🔵 **ADK**               |
| Need maximum workflow control   | 🟢 **LangGraph**         |
| Need model/provider flexibility | 🟢 **LangGraph**         |


=============

LangGraph is excellent when the workflow is the main thing you want to control;

ADK is excellent when the agent ecosystem and Google Cloud/Gemini integration are the main things you want to build around.

